{"version":1,"summary":"scripts/ci vuln scans each module with the exact official Go release its go.mod names.","files":[{"path":"scripts/ci","summary":"vuln() pins GOTOOLCHAIN per module instead of using the local or auto toolchain.","annotations":[{"newRange":[26,29],"summary":"vuln reads the root go.mod Go version and runs govulncheck and its build under that exact toolchain.","rationale":"A distro Go such as go1.27.2-X:nodwarf5 cannot be mapped by govulncheck, so it reported no standard-library findings and passed where CI failed. Verified: with go.mod at 1.27.2 the script exits 3 on GO-2026-6809 while main's script exits 0.","author":"fm/verilex-vuln-toolchain"},{"newRange":[33,35],"summary":"The site/ scan uses the Go version from site/go.mod, read with GOWORK=off, instead of GOTOOLCHAIN=auto.","rationale":"auto resolves to the local suffixed Go, which has the same mapping problem. Verified: with 1.27.3 in all go.mod files the script exits 0. Not tested on a non-suffixed Go.","author":"fm/verilex-vuln-toolchain"}]}]}
